+  - adr: "026"
+    why: >
+      Model-writing plays still write the product model directly. Brief part 1 says writing the
+      product model is the work of the play built for it, not a memory write — this agrees.
+  - adr: "033"
+    why: >
+      The review step still writes approval into the product model from the person's answers.
+      Judgment call: that is a product-model write by the step built for it (brief part 1), not
+      a memory write, so it is not affected.
+  - adr: "030"
+    why: >
+      Names `play-close.md` only for the Pipeline Steps table, and the "converge-and-lint
+      pattern of the Standard Play Close" as a model. It does not decide that the close is
+      copied into each play. Not affected.
+  - adr: "025"
+    why: Lists "Standard Play Close" as part of the evidence contract. Where its text lives is not decided there. Not affected.
+  - adrs: ["028", "031", "032"]
+    why: Overlap candidates by shared words only (/intent, /vision, /understand). Nothing in them is about where memory is read or written.
+no_adr_for_the_close: >
+  No ADR records that the Standard Play Close is copied into every play. That rule lives in
+  `CLAUDE.md` ("Play Pipeline Rules", the durability rule: "/play-creator emits it (gate G12)"),
+  in `core/components/memory/standards/rules/play-close.md`, and in the lint check. Part 9
+  changes those files; there is no older ADR to amend for it.
+
+# ------------------------------------------------------------------
